# Everything the image must NOT contain.
#
# This file is a security control as much as a build optimisation. The two
# entries that matter most are `.env` and `*.pkl`: one is credentials, the other
# is the legacy pickle corpus, and neither may ever be baked into a layer. A
# layer is world-readable to anyone who can pull the image, and deleting a file
# in a later RUN does not remove it from the layer that added it.

# --- Credentials and local configuration -----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
frontend/.env*

# --- The legacy prototype: never in the deployed image ---------------------
# The container serves the API from the `synapse` package. The prototype trees
# and their pickle corpus are development-only, and `*.pkl` is refused outright
# by tests/test_no_pickle_and_imports.py's spirit as well as by size.
*.pkl
Data/
Retrieval/
Generation/
Evaluation/
hybrid_index/
processed_chunks.pkl

# --- The other interface ---------------------------------------------------
# Streamlit is a local fallback and is not installed in this image; shipping its
# entry point would invite someone to try to run it here.
app.py
templates/

# --- Frontend: built and deployed separately (Vercel) ----------------------
frontend/

# --- Build, test and tooling artefacts -------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
artifacts/
evals/
tests/

# --- VCS and editor --------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitleaks*
.DS_Store
.devcontainer/
.claude/
*.md
!README.md
